      "summaries": {
        "en": "Editor is an open-source TypeScript tool that enables users to create and share 3D architectural projects directly in the browser. Its technical strength lies in implementing real-time 3D rendering and collaborative editing capabilities through web technologies, allowing architectural visualization without specialized software. Developers can integrate it into existing workflows or extend its functionality for custom architectural design applications, making professional 3D modeling accessible through standard web interfaces.",
        "zh": "Editor是一款基于TypeScript的开源工具，让用户能够在浏览器中直接创建和分享三维建筑项目。它通过Web技术实现实时三维渲染和协同编辑功能，使建筑可视化无需依赖专业软件即可完成。该项目的核心价值在于将复杂的建筑建模流程简化为网页操作，开发者可将其集成到现有工作流中，或扩展功能用于定制化建筑设计应用，为建筑设计和展示提供了轻量级的技术解决方案。",
        "es": "Editor is an open-source TypeScript tool that enables users to create and share 3D architectural projects directly in the browser. Its technical strength lies in implementing real-time 3D rendering and collaborative editing capabilities through web technologies, allowing architectural visualization without specialized software. Developers can integrate it into existing workflows or extend its functionality for custom architectural design applications, making professional 3D modeling accessible through standard web interfaces.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "editor gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Editor is an open-source TypeScript tool that enables users to create and share 3D architectural projects directly in the browser. Its technical strength lies in implementing real-time 3D rendering and collaborative editing capabilities through web technologies, allowing architectural visualization without specialized software. Developers can integrate it into existing workflows or extend its functionality for custom architectural design applications, making professional 3D modeling accessible through standard web interfaces.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/pascalorg/editor for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
